Practical 5 : Variable Handling

• Write a program to swap two variables (with and without temporary 
variable).

Program 5.1 — Swapping using a temporary variable

code :- 

x = int(input("Enter value of x: "))
y = int(input("Enter value of y: "))
print(f"\nBefore swapping: x = {x}, y = {y}")
temp = x
x = y
y = temp
print(f"After swapping (using temp variable): x = {x}, y = {y}")

output :- 

Enter value of x: 2
Enter value of y: 3
Before swapping: x = 2, y = 3
After swapping (using temp variable): x = 3, y = 2

Program 5.2 — Swapping WITHOUT a temporary variable

code :- 

x = int(input("Enter value of x: "))
y = int(input("Enter value of y: "))
print(f"\nBefore swapping: x = {x}, y = {y}")
# --- Method A: Arithmetic operators ---
x = x + y
y = x - y
x = x - y
print(f"After swapping (arithmetic method): x = {x}, y = {y}")

output :- 

================
Enter value of x: 5 
Enter value of y: 10
Before swapping: x = 5, y = 10
After swapping (arithmetic method): x = 10, y = 5
